{"availability":"available","full":"Pritish-23/TieredFlow","name":"TieredFlow","description":"A Cost & Latency-Optimizing Multi-Agent Orchestrator built with LangGraph","category":"AI & machine learning","language":"Python","stars":0,"forks":0,"created":"2026-07-05T18:57:39Z","updated":"2026-07-18T06:42:18Z","branch":"main","homepage":"https://tieredflow.streamlit.app","topics":["human-in-","langchain","langgraph","llm","multi-agent","python","rag","semantic-cache","streamlit"],"demo":"https://tieredflow.streamlit.app/","color":"#323057","ink":"#d6caff","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-10T09:07:37.556Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-10T09:07:37.556Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-10T09:07:37.556Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-10T09:07:37.556Z","stars":0,"forks":0}],"technologies":["Python"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["A Cost/Latency-Aware Multi-Agent LLM Orchestrator built with LangGraph","TieredFlow intelligently routes user queries across a 4-tier model lineup based on task complexity, live budget, and semantic cache hits — while keeping a human in the loop for every routing decision that matters. It's designed to answer a question every production LLM system eventually has to: when is it worth paying more for a smarter model?","Most LLM demos call one model for everything. TieredFlow instead treats cost, latency, and correctness as first-class constraints, and makes routing decisions transparent and overridable rather than hidden inside a black box:"],"features":["4-tier routing — classifies each query's task type via an LLM classifier, then routes to the cheapest tier that can handle it (ultra-cheap Groq Llama for classification/extraction, up to Claude Sonnet for deep reasoning)","Semantic cache with tiered trust — near-duplicate queries are served from cache automatically at high similarity, prompt a human decision at medium similarity, and skip the cache entirely below that","Full human-in-the-loop (HITL) control — three separate interrupt points (cache-serve decision, tier override, query-rewrite choice) let a human step in before any cost is incurred","Self-correcting hallucination fallback — when a knowledge tool (e.g. Wikipedia) comes up empty, the system automatically falls back to web search combined with the model's own knowledge, rather than either hallucinating…","Confidence scoring — every fresh LLM response is self-scored 1–10 by a second, cheap model call, surfaced directly in the UI"],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/Pritish-23/TieredFlow/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"6b98b2db7024953af60932911bc028c1353fc76e215ab9327f66beb4e73b04c8","extractedAt":"2026-10-10T09:07:37.710Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-10T09:07:37.710Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"A Cost/Latency-Aware Multi-Agent LLM Orchestrator built with LangGraph","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/Pritish-23/TieredFlow/blob/main/README.md"},"audience":[],"requirements":[{"kind":"account","status":"required","text":"Go to share.streamlit.io and sign in with GitHub.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/Pritish-23/TieredFlow/blob/main/README.md"}],"fingerprint":"6b98b2db7024953af60932911bc028c1353fc76e215ab9327f66beb4e73b04c8","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/Pritish-23/TieredFlow/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-10T09:07:37.711Z"},"overviewRepoUpdated":"2026-07-18T06:42:18Z","readmeSnapshot":{"version":1,"status":"saved","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/Pritish-23/TieredFlow/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-10T09:07:37.712Z","hash":"6b98b2db7024953af60932911bc028c1353fc76e215ab9327f66beb4e73b04c8","originalBytes":15484,"storedBytes":15484,"truncated":false,"searchTerms":["cache","query","tier","llm","streamlit","model","cost","api","eval","screenshots","search","settings","before","decision","docs","key","semantic","call","groq","history","hitl","langgraph","tieredflow","wikipedia","anthropic","chat","human","page","session","task","via","web","analytics","both","cloud","config","every","full","hit","latency